# Database & migrations

Source of truth: `docs/database-schema.md` (43 tables). Every ORM model must match that doc.

## Where tables live

| Schema doc section | Model module |
|--------------------|--------------|
| § 1 Auth | `app/models/auth.py` |
| § 2 Profiles | `app/models/profiles.py` |
| § 3 Lookups & tags | `app/models/lookups.py` |
| § 4 Availability | `app/models/availability.py` |
| § 5 Ventor wellness | `app/models/ventor_wellness.py` |
| § 6 Settings | `app/models/settings.py` |
| § 7 Sessions | `app/models/sessions.py` |
| § 8 Earnings | `app/models/earnings.py` |
| § 9 Rewards | `app/models/rewards.py` |
| § 10 Notifications | `app/models/notifications.py` |
| § 11 Training | `app/models/training.py` |
| § 12 Promo | `app/models/promo.py` |

Shared PostgreSQL enums → `app/models/enums.py`.

## Model rules

- Inherit from `app.db.base.Base`; use mixins (`UUIDPrimaryKeyMixin`, `TimestampMixin`, `SoftDeleteMixin`) when they match the schema.
- `__tablename__` = snake_case table name from the doc.
- UUID PKs, `TIMESTAMPTZ` for datetimes, `NUMERIC(12,2)` for money.
- Register new modules in `app/models/__init__.py` so Alembic autogenerate sees them.
- Do not put business logic in models — only columns, relationships, indexes.

## Migrations workflow

```bash
# after adding/changing models
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "profiles: ventor and listener tables"
alembic upgrade head
```

- One migration per domain batch when possible (e.g. auth, then profiles).
- Review autogenerated diffs before committing.
- Never edit applied migrations — add a new revision instead.

## DB access in API

```python
from app.api.deps import DbSession

def my_route(db: DbSession):
    ...
```

Services receive `Session`; routers inject via `DbSession`.
